.page kappasay 1 let a kappa say something

# SYNOPSIS
*kappasay* [*-nt*] [*-W* _COLUMNS_] [_TEXT_...]

# DESCRIPTION
`kappasay` is reimusay(1) with a different speaker: a kappa from the workshop of Nitori's toolbox, dish on her head and cucumber at hand. The options are the same: text from the arguments or standard input, wrapped to 40 columns.

# OPTIONS
@ *-W* _COLUMNS_
    Wrap the text at _COLUMNS_ instead of 40.
@ *-n*
    Keep the input lines unwrapped.
@ *-t*
    A thought bubble.

# EXAMPLES
    kappasay "Have you tried turning it off and on again?"
    uname -a | kappasay -n

# SEE ALSO
reimusay(1), kappabox(1)
